Now I understand the Dart test patterns. Note the existing test: "a dangling summary (request died mid-flight) still counts, marked estimated" — expects `byModel[unknownUsageModel]` isNotNull. With my change, the fallback will now carry an estimated input (from chars), so that test still passes (it only asserts byModel presence). 

